Config `ai.population...` presumably resolves via AiSettings (the YAML-backed settings) — `AiSettings::population` etc. Let me check AiSettings line ~131 to see whether the config tree 'ai' comes from a file resources/settings YAML... Actually maybe the module has a `config/ai.php`? We listed config/: campaign-consultation.php, cognition.php, config.php, horizon.php, language.php, population.php, pricing.php, review.php, routing.php. Nwidart ModuleServiceProvider loads config files and merges them under the module's alias: In nwidart/laravel-modules, `ModuleServiceProvider` (Support\ModuleServiceProvider) registers config as `config()->set($moduleNameLower.'.'.$key)`? Let me check vendor nwidart's ModuleServiceProvider: it typically calls `$this->mergeConfigFrom($path, strtolower($this->name))`? If it merges each file's contents under... hmm, actually it does:

```php
foreach ($this->getConfigFiles() as $key => $path) {
    $this->mergeConfigFrom($path, $key);
}
```
where `getConfigFiles()` returns [filename-without-extension => path]? If the key were the filename, config('population.dispatch_batch_size'). But the module uses 'ai.population...'. Hmm, in nwidart, `ModuleServiceProvider::registerConfiguration()`:

```php
    protected function registerConfiguration(): void
    {
        if ($this->app['config']->get('modules.auto-load-config', true)) {
            foreach ($this->getConfigFiles() as $key => $path) {
                $this->mergeConfigFrom($path, $key);
            }
        }
    }
```
and `getConfigFiles()` returns `Finder::create()->files()->in($this->getModulePath().'/config')` keyed by filename sans extension? Hmm... In newer versions:
```php
foreach ($this->getConfigFiles() as $key => $path) {
    $this->mergeConfigFrom($path, $key);
}
...
private function getConfigFiles(): array
{
    $files = [];
    foreach ($this->getConfigDirectories() as $directory) {
        foreach ((new Finder)->files()->name('*.php')->in($directory) as $file) {
            $files[$file->getFilenameWithoutExtension()] = $file->getRealPath();
        }
    }
    ...
```
That yields key 'population'. Hmm, that contradicts too. Unless the module sets `protected string $nameLower = 'ai';` and there's a custom override... Let me search vendor for ModuleServiceProvider config handling, or check AiSettings which might map the YAML to config('ai.*'). Let's look at AiSettings.

